  2220	### Custom Rendering
  2221	
  2222	Tools can provide `renderCall` and `renderResult` for custom TUI display. See [tui.md](tui.md) for the full component API and [tool-execution.ts](https://github.com/earendil-works/pi-mono/blob/main/packages/coding-agent/src/modes/interactive/components/tool-execution.ts) for how tool rows are composed.
  2223	
  2224	By default, tool output is wrapped in a `Box` that handles padding and background. A defined `renderCall` or `renderResult` must return a `Component`. If a slot renderer is not defined, `tool-execution.ts` uses fallback rendering for that slot.
  2225	
  2226	Set `renderShell: "self"` when the tool should render its own shell instead of using the default `Box`. This is useful for tools that need complete control over framing or background behavior, for example large previews that must stay visually stable after the tool settles.
  2227	
  2228	```typescript
  2229	pi.registerTool({
  2230	  name: "my_tool",
  2231	  label: "My Tool",
  2232	  description: "Custom shell example",
  2233	  parameters: Type.Object({}),
  2234	  renderShell: "self",
  2235	  async execute() {
  2236	    return { content: [{ type: "text", text: "ok" }], details: undefined };
  2237	  },
  2238	  renderCall(args, theme, context) {
  2239	    return new Text(theme.fg("accent", "my custom shell"), 0, 0);
  2240	  },
  2241	});
  2242	```
  2243	
  2244	`renderCall` and `renderResult` each receive a `context` object with:
  2245	- `args` - the current tool call arguments
  2246	- `state` - shared row-local state across `renderCall` and `renderResult`
  2247	- `lastComponent` - the previously returned component for that slot, if any
  2248	- `invalidate()` - request a rerender of this tool row
  2249	- `toolCallId`, `cwd`, `executionStarted`, `argsComplete`, `isPartial`, `expanded`, `showImages`, `isError`
  2250	
  2251	Use `context.state` for cross-slot shared state. Keep slot-local caches on the returned component instance when you want to reuse and mutate the same component across renders.
  2252	
  2253	#### renderCall
  2254	
  2255	Renders the tool call or header:
