  2298	#### Keybinding Hints
  2299	
  2300	Use `keyHint()` to display keybinding hints that respect the active keybinding configuration:
  2301	
  2302	```typescript
  2303	import { keyHint } from "@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent";
  2304	
  2305	renderResult(result, { expanded }, theme, context) {
  2306	  let text = theme.fg("success", "✓ Done");
  2307	  if (!expanded) {
  2308	    text += ` (${keyHint("app.tools.expand", "to expand")})`;
  2309	  }
  2310	  return new Text(text, 0, 0);
  2311	}
  2312	```
  2313	
  2314	Available functions:
  2315	- `keyHint(keybinding, description)` - Formats a configured keybinding id such as `"app.tools.expand"` or `"tui.select.confirm"`
  2316	- `keyText(keybinding)` - Returns the raw configured key text for a keybinding id
  2317	- `rawKeyHint(key, description)` - Format a raw key string
  2318	
  2319	Use namespaced keybinding ids:
  2320	- Coding-agent ids use the `app.*` namespace, for example `app.tools.expand`, `app.editor.external`, `app.session.rename`
  2321	- Shared TUI ids use the `tui.*` namespace, for example `tui.select.confirm`, `tui.select.cancel`, `tui.input.tab`
  2322	
  2323	For the exhaustive list of keybinding ids and defaults, see [keybindings.md](keybindings.md). `keybindings.json` uses those same namespaced ids.
  2324	
  2325	Custom editors and `ctx.ui.custom()` components receive `keybindings: KeybindingsManager` as an injected argument. They should use that injected manager directly instead of calling `getKeybindings()` or `setKeybindings()`.
  2326	
  2327	#### Best Practices
  2328	
  2329	- Use `Text` with padding `(0, 0)`. The default Box handles padding.
  2330	- Use `\n` for multi-line content.
  2331	- Handle `isPartial` for streaming progress.
  2332	- Support `expanded` for detail on demand.
  2333	- Keep default view compact.
  2334	- Read `context.args` in `renderResult` instead of copying args into `context.state`.
  2335	- Use `context.state` only for data that must be shared across call and result slots.
  2336	- Reuse `context.lastComponent` when the same component instance can be updated in place.
  2337	- Use `renderShell: "self"` only when the default boxed shell gets in the way. In self-shell mode the tool is responsible for its own framing, padding, and background.
  2338	
  2339	#### Fallback
  2340	
  2341	If a slot renderer is not defined or throws:
  2342	- `renderCall`: Shows the tool name
  2343	- `renderResult`: Shows raw text from `content`
